    },
    "body": "current-state.md records the serving result (0.93277 BPB, 4.70x) but not the binding line that followed it. This adds it: the no-pointer control at 0/84 against the pointer at 35/84; a serving-time gate floor recovering exact recall of never-seen values on every arm with zero cells lost (49/84, 59/84 = 0.7024, 52/84) with span and read mass bit-identical across the floor, so the floor moves only the mixing weight; termination as the residual failure (value present in 79/84 at F=1.0 but 6/84 exact); the run-length stop at 65/84 = 0.7738 which fires on the prompt template (span inside the value's own span on only 20 of 79); and the token-identity stop at a NEW BEST 72/84 = 0.8571 [0.7667, 0.9163] that also recovers F=1.0 from 6 to 71. Significance is stated honestly: against 65/84 the Newcombe interval CONTAINS ZERO (p=0.0654), so it is a better point estimate and not significant on 84 cells, while it is significant against the 59/84 plateau (p=0.00235). Limits recorded: the mechanism is 'end the reply at the end of the first span the pointer sustains by token identity', not 'recognise the value'; extra fine-tuning alone costs about 13 points, so extend-the-run is retracted for this axis; and the whole line is OFFLINE ONLY because export refuses a pointer with an identity term - no integer port - so it must never be reported as served. Also records the defect this work exposed: #2009 landed half the copy-stop change and main could not compile its lib tests until #2040. References #820",
